OL,3,GNEWSA'Ketamine is destroying young     
OL,4,Apeople's lives'                        
OL,6,FA surgeon who treats ketamine addicts  
OL,7,Fsays she is "overwhelmed" by the number
OL,8,Fof teenagers and young adults with     
OL,9,Fbladders so damaged by the drug that   
OL,10,Fthey need major reconstructive surgery.
OL,12,FAlison Downey, who is based at         
OL,13,FPinderfields Hospital in Wakefield,    
OL,14,Fsays some of her patients require the  
OL,15,Fsort of treatment normally given to    
OL,16,Fcancer sufferers.                      
OL,18,FThe use of the Class B drug by young   
OL,19,Fpeople has increased dramatically.     
OL,20,FNationally it rose by 231% among 16-24 
OL,21,Fyear-olds in the 11 years up to 2024.  
